1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,648
This course uses fictional
evidence and a local prototype.

2
00:00:03,718 --> 00:00:08,838
You will practice a complete delivery loop while
maintaining the distinction between simulated

3
00:00:08,908 --> 00:00:10,295
and field evidence.

4
00:00:10,365 --> 00:00:13,799
Each lesson produces something
that feeds the next decision.

5
00:00:13,869 --> 00:00:19,203
Keep a dated journal, store your first
prediction before examining later evidence, and

6
00:00:19,273 --> 00:00:21,769
separate your submission
from the worked solution.

7
00:00:21,839 --> 00:00:25,273
Completion can demonstrate
learning in this environment.

8
00:00:25,343 --> 00:00:31,573
Production competence also requires experience
with real constraints, users, ownership, and

9
00:00:31,643 --> 00:00:32,859
consequences.

10
00:00:32,929 --> 00:00:37,174
Northstar has a fictional baseline
of 20 minutes per ticket review.

11
00:00:37,244 --> 00:00:39,548
A later sample reports 12 minutes.

12
00:00:39,618 --> 00:00:43,095
These values exist for practicing
measurement and judgment.

13
00:00:43,165 --> 00:00:47,944
They are neither market benchmarks
nor promises about AI productivity.

14
00:00:48,014 --> 00:00:52,793
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

15
00:00:52,863 --> 00:00:58,644
Create a dated learning journal with headings
for evidence, assumptions, predictions, observed

16
00:00:58,714 --> 00:01:00,207
results, and decisions.

17
00:01:00,277 --> 00:01:05,504
A useful first entry says: known within
the case, twenty agents handle three ticket

18
00:01:05,574 --> 00:01:10,075
categories. Assumed, routing
suggestions will save review time.

19
00:01:10,145 --> 00:01:13,303
Unknown, whether agents
will use them consistently.

20
00:01:13,373 --> 00:01:18,535
Next action, observe a simulated review
and test one end-to-end suggestion.

21
00:01:18,605 --> 00:01:21,507
No real customer outcome has been established.

22
00:01:21,577 --> 00:01:25,054
Preserve this entry when later
evidence changes your view.

23
00:01:25,124 --> 00:01:27,257
How should you describe the sample numbers?

24
00:01:27,327 --> 00:01:29,802
A. Verified industry benchmarks B.

25
00:01:29,872 --> 00:01:32,048
Guaranteed productivity gains C.

26
00:01:32,118 --> 00:01:34,230
Fictional data for an exercise.

27
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:35,708
The best answer is C.

28
00:01:35,778 --> 00:01:38,487
The case is an educational simulation.

29
00:01:38,557 --> 00:01:41,459
Do not convert its values into commercial proof.
